  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1/3 — Fixed barrel shifter cascade bug (dut_bug). Root cause: stages 2–5 (tmp2–tmp5) used tmp0 instead of the previous stage's output in their active rotation branches, so only the largest active rotation was applied instead of cumulative rotation. Fixed 4 lines: line 39 (tmp2 uses tmp1), line 46 (tmp3 uses tmp2), line 53 (tmp4 uses tmp3), line 60 (tmp5 uses tmp4). This directly addresses the causal path: chaining through previous stage outputs ensures each rotation amount accumulates correctly. The fix resolves all three failing properties (barrel_shifter_correct_rotation, load_mode_output_correct, spinning_progress) since all depend on correct cascaded rotation. All assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Round 2/3 — Fixed assertion timing mismatch (assertion_error). Root cause: assertion `load_mode_output_correct` at line 110 compared registered `doutReg` (rotation of *previous-cycle* `inrReg`) with combinational `s5` (rotation of *current-cycle* `inrReg`) in the same cycle, causing a one-cycle pipeline mismatch. Fix: changed `doutReg === s5` to `doutReg === RegNext(s5)` to snapshot the reference value from the previous cycle, matching the pipeline delay of `doutReg`. The assertion label `load_mode_output_correct` is preserved. No homologous assertions found — only one `assertImplies` exists in the source.",
    "Round 3/3 — Fixed assertion predicate for `spinning_progress` (assertion_error). Root cause: the `astRelaxedLiveness` start condition `splReg && io.amount =/= 0.U` did not account for the identity case where the value being rotated is zero. Rotating 0 by any non-zero amount always yields 0, so `io.dout =/= RegNext(io.dout)` can never be satisfied when `doutReg=0`. Fix: added `&& doutReg =/= 0.U` to the start condition at line 107 (original). This directly addresses the causal path: a zero-valued output cannot change under rotation because `rotate_left(0, k) = 0` for any k, making the progress condition vacuously unachievable. The assertion label `spinning_progress` is preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions — only one `astRelaxedLiveness` exists in the source."
  ],
